{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1988","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Split the Multiset"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"512 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"multiset"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is a set of numbers in which there can be equal elements, and the order of the numbers does not matter. For example, $$$\\{2,2,4\\}$$$ is a multiset."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You have a multiset $$$S$$$. Initially, the multiset contains only one positive integer $$$n$$$. That is, $$$S=\\{n\\}$$$. Additionally, there is a given positive integer $$$k$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In one operation, you can select any positive integer $$$u$$$ in $$$S$$$ and remove one copy of $$$u$$$ from $$$S$$$. Then, insert no more than $$$k$$$ positive integers into $$$S$$$ so that the sum of all inserted integers is equal to $$$u$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Find the minimum number of operations to make $$$S$$$ contain $$$n$$$ ones."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 1000$$$). Description of the test cases follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only line of each testcase contains two integers $$$n,k$$$ ($$$1\\le n\\le 1000,2\\le k\\le 1000$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each testcase, print one integer, which is the required answer."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n1 5\n5 2\n6 3\n16 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n0\n4\n3\n5\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For the first test case, initially $$$S=\\{1\\}$$$, already satisfying the requirement. Therefore, we need zero operations."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For the second test case, initially $$$S=\\{5\\}$$$. We can apply the following operations:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Select $$$u=5$$$, remove $$$u$$$ from $$$S$$$, and insert $$$2,3$$$ into $$$S$$$. Now, $$$S=\\{2,3\\}$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Select $$$u=2$$$, remove $$$u$$$ from $$$S$$$, and insert $$$1,1$$$ into $$$S$$$. Now, $$$S=\\{1,1,3\\}$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Select $$$u=3$$$, remove $$$u$$$ from $$$S$$$, and insert $$$1,2$$$ into $$$S$$$. Now, $$$S=\\{1,1,1,2\\}$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Select $$$u=2$$$, remove $$$u$$$ from $$$S$$$, and insert $$$1,1$$$ into $$$S$$$. Now, $$$S=\\{1,1,1,1,1\\}$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Using $$$4$$$ operations in total, we achieve the goal."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For the third test case, initially $$$S=\\{6\\}$$$. We can apply the following operations:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Select $$$u=6$$$, remove $$$u$$$ from $$$S$$$, and insert $$$1,2,3$$$ into $$$S$$$. Now, $$$S=\\{1,2,3\\}$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Select $$$u=2$$$, remove $$$u$$$ from $$$S$$$, and insert $$$1,1$$$ into $$$S$$$. Now, $$$S=\\{1,1,1,3\\}$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Select $$$u=3$$$, remove $$$u$$$ from $$$S$$$, and insert $$$1,1,1$$$ into $$$S$$$. Now, $$$S=\\{1,1,1,1,1,1\\}$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Using $$$3$$$ operations in total, we achieve the goal."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For the fourth test case, initially $$$S=\\{16\\}$$$. We can apply the following operations:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Select $$$u=16$$$, remove $$$u$$$ from $$$S$$$, and insert $$$4,4,4,4$$$ into $$$S$$$. Now, $$$S=\\{4,4,4,4\\}$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Repeat for $$$4$$$ times: select $$$u=4$$$, remove $$$u$$$ from $$$S$$$, and insert $$$1,1,1,1$$$ into $$$S$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Using $$$5$$$ operations in total, we achieve the goal."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"1988A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1988/problem/A"}